  { name: 'Ruen Pair', locs: [L('Thai Town', 34.10206, -118.3055)] },
  { name: 'NAM Kitchen', locs: [L('Gardena', 33.87261, -118.30354)] },
  { name: '71Above', locs: [L('Downtown', 34.05115, -118.25455)] },
  { name: 'Bestia', locs: [L('Arts District', 34.03371, -118.22921)] },
  { name: 'Nobu', locs: [L('La Cienega', 34.0862, -118.3765)] },
  { name: 'Tesla Diner', locs: [L('Hollywood', 34.09095, -118.34188)] },
  { name: "Geoffrey's", locs: [L('Malibu', 34.02521, -118.7699)] },
];
const OC = [
  { name: 'Shake Shack', locs: [L('Crystal Cove', 33.57396, -117.83947)] },
  { name: 'Urth Caffé', locs: [L('Laguna Beach', 33.54421, -117.78843)] },
  { name: 'Splashes', locs: [L('Laguna Beach', 33.53024, -117.77387)] },
  { name: 'Circle Hook Fish Co.', locs: [L('Newport Beach', 33.61904, -117.9284)] },
  { name: 'OC & Lau', locs: [L('Garden Grove', 33.77324, -117.95609)] },
  { name: 'Gyu-Kaku', locs: [L('Tustin', 33.73469, -117.82596)] },
  { name: 'Northern Cafe', locs: [L('Irvine', 33.68336, -117.81314)] },
  { name: 'Hako', locs: [L('Irvine', 33.71236, -117.7613)] },
  { name: 'King Chops', locs: [L('Irvine', 33.68095, -117.77887)] },
  { name: 'Mendocino Farms', locs: [L('Irvine', 33.65083, -117.83915)] },
  { name: 'Postino', locs: [L('Irvine', 33.67294, -117.84662)] },
  { name: 'Prime Hot Pot', locs: [L('Irvine', 33.69808, -117.82856)] },
  { name: 'Agora Churrascaria', locs: [L('Irvine', 33.68536, -117.85619)] },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Eating Out — Huanyu Chen"
  description="Restaurants, 2022–2026, region by region: sizzling pots and Shanghainese in the San Gabriel Valley, brunch and Thai Town in Los Angeles, burgers at sunset and Lao food in Orange County, and a few big dinners, each with a map.">
  <p class="muted"><a href="/misc">← Misc</a> · 2022 – 2026</p>
  <h1>Eating Out</h1>
  <p class="muted trip-sub">The restaurants we keep going back to, and a few dinners we only had once.</p>

  <div class="callout trip-stats">
    <strong>4 years · April 2022 – November 2026</strong><br />
    clay pot rice and red-braised pork · Mongolian lamb in a painted pot · eggs and salad on the Urth patio ·
    burgers over the ocean at sunset · snails on a sizzling plate · s'mores on a yakiniku grill · octopus on the
    71st floor · paella on a Malibu cliff
  </div>

  <p>
    This is the savory half of the sweets post. It is shorter, because a meal is a bigger decision than a drink:
    the places below are the ones that show up again and again in the photos, plus a handful of dinners that were
    worth the occasion.
  </p>
  <p>
    The post goes region by region, each with a map. Most of the photos are from my wife's camera roll, taken before
    anyone picked up a fork; the special dinners at the end are mostly from mine.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sgv">San Gabriel Valley</h2>
  <p>
    The Chinese food is here, along Valley Boulevard in San Gabriel and up Baldwin Avenue in Arcadia.
  </p>
  <RegionMap stores={SGV} region="the San Gabriel Valley" />
  <p>
    One plaza on Valley Boulevard in San Gabriel, where most of the boba in the sweets post comes from, has two of the
    regulars. <strong>Nature Pagoda</strong> does clay pot rice. <strong>Ikka Sizzling Pot</strong>, a few doors
    down, does set meals in red-rimmed bowls with rice and pickles on the side.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'ikka-stew.webp'} alt="Clay pot rice topped with braised beef, broccoli and peppers." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Clay pot rice, Nature Pagoda, San Gabriel, March 2023.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'ikka-table.webp'} alt="A red-rimmed noodle bowl with a bowl of rice and a side of pickled vegetables." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Ikka Sizzling Pot, June 2026.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    In Arcadia, <strong>Auntie Qiu Kitchen</strong> does Shanghainese food: red-braised pork belly with eggs, and a pot
    of noodles with seaweed and tofu skin.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'auntie-qiu-pork.webp'} alt="Glossy red-braised pork belly with braised eggs on a white plate." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Red-braised pork, Auntie Qiu Kitchen, Arcadia, July 2023.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'auntie-qiu-noodles.webp'} alt="An enamel pot of noodles in broth with seaweed, greens and tofu skin." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Noodles in the pot, April 2026.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    A few blocks east, <strong>Mo-Mo Paradise</strong> is shabu-shabu, with a pot for each person.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'mo-mo.webp'} alt="Two shabu-shabu pots on a table with plates of sliced meat, greens and dipping sauces." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Mo-Mo Paradise, Arcadia, February 2023.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    Two doors apart on Baldwin Avenue are <strong>Hodori BBQ</strong>, Korean barbecue with a grill in the middle of the
    table, and <strong>Tai Er</strong>, whose pickled-cabbage fish comes in a bowl the size of a steering wheel.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'hodori.webp'} alt="A Korean barbecue table with a round grill, spicy pork in a skillet and small side dishes." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Hodori BBQ, Arcadia, September 2024.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'tai-er.webp'} alt="A large white bowl of fish in yellow pickled-cabbage broth with chilies, next to a plate of stir-fried greens." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Tai Er, Arcadia, October 2024.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    <strong>Dong Ting Chun</strong> on Valley Boulevard is Hunan food, heavy on the peppers.
    <strong>Lunasia</strong> in Pasadena is the dim sum: har gow topped with fish roe in black dishes.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'dong-ting-chun.webp'} alt="A dark plate of stir-fried pork with green and red peppers." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Dong Ting Chun, San Gabriel, December 2025.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'lunasia.webp'} alt="Dumplings topped with orange fish roe in black shell-shaped dishes in a steamer." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Lunasia, Pasadena, March 2023.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    Further east in Rowland Heights, <strong>Guangfa Grassland</strong> serves Inner Mongolian food: lamb and sausage
    simmered in a pot painted with yurts, and a plate that is more dried chili than anything else.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'guangfa-pot.webp'} alt="A metal pot painted blue with white yurts, full of lamb and greens in broth." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The yurt pot, Guangfa Grassland, Rowland Heights, April 2024.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'guangfa-chili.webp'} alt="A plate piled with dried red chilies and fried meat." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The chili plate.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    And one we never learned the name of: a whole roast leg of lamb, Xinjiang style, in a plaza in Alhambra in July 2022.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'lamb-leg.webp'} alt="A whole roast leg of lamb on a foil-lined tray, topped with cilantro and carrots." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Roast lamb leg, Alhambra, July 16, 2022.</figcaption></figure>

  <h2 id="la">Los Angeles</h2>
  <p>
    In the rest of Los Angeles the regulars are brunch places, and Thai Town.
  </p>
  <RegionMap stores={LA} region="Los Angeles" />
  <p>
    <strong>Urth Caffé</strong> in the Arts District is the one we go to most (the card records show about ten
    visits to Urth across its shops): eggs, salad and a slab of bread on the patio.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'urth-dtla.webp'} alt="Baked eggs in tomato sauce with salad and bread, a slice of cake behind." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Urth Caffé, Arts District, July 2023.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'urth-dtla-eggs.webp'} alt="Scrambled eggs with tomato, a salad and a round of bread on an outdoor table." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Back in October 2023.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    <strong>Gracias Madre</strong> in West Hollywood is plant-based Mexican food, served on long tables in the
    afternoon sun.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'gracias-madre.webp'} alt="A bowl of avocado and hearts of palm ceviche with chilies." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Gracias Madre, West Hollywood, June 2023.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'gracias-madre-table.webp'} alt="A table covered in plates in afternoon sun, with a flatbread in front." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The whole table, July 2023.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    <strong>République</strong> on La Brea is the brunch for an occasion. The first visit, in September 2022, was eggs
    Benedict and a berry cake from the pastry case.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'republique-benedict.webp'} alt="Eggs Benedict on thick toast with hollandaise and avocado." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>République, September 20, 2022.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'republique-cake.webp'} alt="A layered cake with cream and fresh berries on a gold board." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The berry cake.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    Later visits were a thick brioche French toast and a stew with a baguette for dipping.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'republique-toast.webp'} alt="A thick caramelized slice of French toast with a small pitcher of syrup and a bowl of fruit." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>French toast, January 2024.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'republique-stew.webp'} alt="A cast-iron pan of stew with two halves of baguette." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Stew and baguette, June 2023.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    <strong>Ruen Pair</strong> in Thai Town, open late, is crispy pork over rice with a dish of chili sauce. Down in
    Gardena, <strong>NAM Kitchen</strong> makes Vietnamese noodle soups.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'ruen-pair.webp'} alt="Crispy pork with cilantro over rice, with a small bowl of chili sauce." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Ruen Pair, Thai Town, January 2024.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'nam.webp'} alt="Two bowls of noodle soup with herbs on a metal mesh table." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>NAM Kitchen, Gardena, February 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h2 id="oc">Orange County</h2>
  <p>
    In Orange County it is the coast, a stretch of Irvine shopping centers, and Garden Grove.
  </p>
  <RegionMap stores={OC} region="Orange County" />
  <p>
    The <strong>Shake Shack</strong> at Crystal Cove sits on the bluff above the Pacific Coast Highway, and the best
    tables face the ocean. It is the same burger as anywhere else, eaten at sunset.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'shake-shack.webp'} alt="A burger and fries in paper on a wooden ledge with the ocean behind in late sun." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Shake Shack, Crystal Cove, November 2023.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'shake-shack-sunset.webp'} alt="The sun setting over the ocean behind a headland, with burger wrappers on the ledge." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Sunset from the same ledge, May 2026.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    Wangcai comes to the patio places. At the <strong>Urth Caffé</strong> in Laguna Beach and at
    <strong>Circle Hook Fish Co.</strong> in Newport Beach, he gets a seat with a view of the fish tacos.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'urth-laguna.webp'} alt="A white dog sitting by an outdoor table with a plate of salad and a wrap." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Urth Caffé, Laguna Beach, May 2026.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'circle-hook.webp'} alt="A white dog behind a tray of fish tacos on a waterfront table." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Circle Hook Fish Co., Newport Beach, January 2026.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    <strong>OC &amp; Lau</strong> in Garden Grove is Lao and Thai food on sizzling iron plates: snails with herbs, and a
    seafood hot pot on a burner.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'oc-lau-snails.webp'} alt="Snails on a sizzling iron plate topped with sprigs of herbs." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>OC &amp; Lau, Garden Grove, March 2026.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'oc-lau-pot.webp'} alt="A metal pot of seafood in red broth over a blue gas flame." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The hot pot, September 2024.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    In Irvine the short list starts with <strong>Northern Cafe</strong> for lamb skewers and <strong>Hako</strong>
    for katsu.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'northern-cafe-r.webp'} alt="A wooden tray of grilled skewers: lamb, green beans and a sausage." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Skewers, Northern Cafe, Irvine, July 2025.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'hako-katsu-r.webp'} alt="A pork katsu set with shredded cabbage, rice, curry and pickles." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Katsu, Hako, Irvine, November 2024.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    Hako's stir-fried udon is the other order. <strong>King Chops</strong> does Taiwanese pork chop rice.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'hako-udon.webp'} alt="A plate of stir-fried udon with beef and green onion." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Stir-fried udon at Hako, May 2025.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'king-chops-r.webp'} alt="A bowl of rice with minced pork, cabbage, broccoli and an egg, next to a fried pork chop and a soup." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>King Chops, Irvine, May 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    And <strong>Mendocino Farms</strong> is for the days that call for a salad.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'mendocino.webp'} alt="A salad with roasted vegetables, fruit and a soft cheese in a dark bowl." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Mendocino Farms, Irvine, July 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    For an evening out there is <strong>Postino</strong>, a wine bar with boards of bread, cheese and olives.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'postino-board.webp'} alt="A wooden board of flatbread, olives, cheese and cured meat beside glasses of white wine." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Postino, Irvine, April 2026.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'postino-dates.webp'} alt="A small dish of stuffed dates in red pepper sauce." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Postino, December 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    At <strong>Gyu-Kaku</strong> in Tustin you grill the beef yourself and finish by toasting marshmallows over the
    same grill.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'gyu-kaku.webp'} alt="Beef sizzling on a round charcoal grill with shishito peppers beside it." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Gyu-Kaku, Tustin, March 2025.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'gyu-kaku-smores.webp'} alt="A marshmallow on a skewer toasting over a round grill." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>S'mores on the same grill.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    <strong>Prime Hot Pot</strong> in Irvine is the hot pot.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'prime-hot-pot.webp'} alt="Trays of thinly sliced beef next to a divided hot pot." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Prime Hot Pot, Irvine, September 2025.</figcaption></figure>

  <h2 id="occasions">Big dinners</h2>
  <p>
    And the meals that were an occasion. They are on the maps above too.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>71Above</strong> is on the 71st floor of the U.S. Bank Tower downtown. In April 2022 dinner started at sunset,
    with grilled octopus, and the city below turned gold as the sun went down.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'above71-octopus.webp'} alt="Grilled octopus with purple potatoes and carrots on a white plate." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Octopus, 71Above, April 9, 2022.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'above71-view.webp'} alt="Looking down on downtown Los Angeles towers from a high window at sunset." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The view from the table.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    <strong>Bestia</strong>, in the Arts District, in August 2023: a blistered Neapolitan pizza and a plate of pasta.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'bestia-pizza-r.webp'} alt="A Neapolitan pizza with charred crust, tomato and mozzarella." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Bestia, August 21, 2023.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'bestia-pasta-r.webp'} alt="A swirl of pasta with herbs in a wide white bowl." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The pasta.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    <strong>Nobu</strong> on La Cienega, in April 2024: yellowtail with jalapeño, shishito peppers and wagyu tacos.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'nobu-yellowtail-r.webp'} alt="Thin slices of yellowtail with jalapeño in ponzu, arranged in a star." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Yellowtail jalapeño, Nobu, April 23, 2024.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'nobu-tacos-r.webp'} alt="Blistered shishito peppers above a slate of small tacos." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Shishitos and wagyu tacos.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    In 2025 there were three more. <strong>Agora Churrascaria</strong> in Irvine in May, where the waiters keep bringing
    meat on skewers until you turn your card over. <strong>Splashes</strong>, at the Surf &amp; Sand in Laguna Beach, in
    June.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'agora.webp'} alt="A plate of carved steak, sausage and sides with a basket of cheese bread." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Agora Churrascaria, Irvine, May 2025.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'splashes.webp'} alt="Four small plated courses on a white tablecloth." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Splashes, Laguna Beach, June 18, 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    And <strong>Geoffrey's</strong> in Malibu at the end of June: paella on a terrace above the Pacific Coast Highway.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'geoffreys-paella.webp'} alt="A plate of seafood paella with shrimp and mussels." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Paella, Geoffrey's, Malibu, June 29, 2025.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'geoffreys-view.webp'} alt="The ocean seen between two umbrellas over a terrace with flowers and cliffside houses." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The terrace.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    Last, the <strong>Tesla Diner</strong> in Hollywood, two days after it opened in July 2025: a chrome drive-in with
    movie screens, where the food is ordered from the car.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'tesla-diner.webp'} alt="A round, chrome, two-story diner building under a blue sky." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The Tesla Diner, Hollywood, July 23, 2025.</figcaption></figure>

  <p class="muted"><small>Photo locations have been removed from the published images. Map pins mark the restaurants
    themselves, mostly from OpenStreetMap. Visit counts come from our own records and only count the times we paid by
    card.</small></p>
  <Comments />
</BaseLayout>
